This is the game I posted about asking for help earlier in the week.
Thank you all for the help --- apparently, it worked. :)

I'd been reading about how daggers were the new rock and roll, and was
originally skeptical. And, while I didn't use the daggers all that much
in Gehennom and onward, they were _instrumental_ in early and mid-game,
and helped me take out a couple of demon princes to boot. But, to start
at the beginning...

This game was full of mistakes. There was a Wand of Wishing on DL3,
which I got distressingly little benefit out of. First, I wished for 2
blessed scrolls of charging, got one. Then, without trying to wish again,
I charged the wand. What was I thinking?? I don't know. Well, whatever,
I said to myself, and wished up AoLS, CoMR, and GoP. I already had a
shield of reflection I had randomly found, and decided I would hope for
scale drop to get my *DSM. I was wearing... a +2 mithril-coat I think?
I think it was the right decision, though I soon afterward found a random
CoMR, enchanted higher than mine. I guess mine was fixed at least...

The Gauntlets of Power turned out to be the only wish that didn't go
toward fixing a mistake; they let me carry around a bunch of daggers
and still some other things until I finally got a bag of holding.
Minetown had a coaligned altar, but I already had a couple of those
in the main dungeon, so I mostly just used this for buc-IDing things.
No magic lamps, but I did find one in the Mines somewhere else, so I
blessed it (holy water was not a problem for me all game). I intended
to use it as a permanent light source...

Sokoban was no big thing, and daggers really are great for getting rid of
monsters behind boulders (though you do lose a couple, so don't use your
enchanted stack. "Oopa"). Around DL12 I made my next big mistake--- ran
into a cockatrice, felt myself slowing down, and rather than immediately
eating one of the _three_ lizard corpses I was carrying, figured "Oh,
I'll just smack it down and then eat it." Goodbye AoLS number 1. I
wrested the last charge from my wand and got another AoLS, and put it on.

I found a couple of bones files that were mostly boring but gave me
Excalibur and Vorpal Blade, which I bagged for a long time and then left
behind in Vlad's tower. It was nice to know that no player monsters
on Astral would be packing Vorpal, though I wish there had been fewer
artifacts generated so I could have wished for Magicbane.

At dl15 I found a coaligned altar and had a sac-fest, ending up with
Werebane, like 15 potions of holy water, and crowning. This gave
me Stormbringer --- ooh shiny! --- which made my life wonderful and
miserable the rest of the game. I accidentally killed four shopkeepers,
dozens of elves, a pile of ogre lords... You might have noticed by now
that I am a poor typist :)

Then (and this will be familiar if you read my previous posts about this
game) I made my way down pretty quickly, and at DL 21, I said "Ooh, I have
an idea! I will sacrifice my own race to get peaceful Jubilex, and then
Gehennom will be easier!" Well, yes, it turned out that that happened, but
it was purely coincidence...

I sacrificed a soldier or something, got Yeenoghu, and said "Awesome! Now
all I need is another human corpse!" And of course "The black blade lashes
out and hits Yeenoghu! Yeenoghu gets angry!" Yeenoghu gated in Demogorgon,
I zapped myself with a wand of teleport, and ended up in a room with
(still) Yeenoghu, Demogorgon, a leocrotta, and a couple of other serious
beasts.  Goodbye AoLS number 2. I should have just wished up a cockatrice
corpse right away with my blessed magic lamp, probably, but I ended up
first levelporting (I didn't have a cursed scroll of teleportation, but
confused and uncursed will do, and one of Yeenoghu and Demogorgon confused
me), and having only Demogorgon follow. I wished up the rubber chicken,
zonked him, and used my unicorn horn. Phew. At this point I decided it
was time to get som intrinsic protection, and while vault-looting, to my
great joy I discovered Ludios, which I had never previously encountered.

Ludios didn't give me SDSM, but it did give me GDSM, which was better AC
and better weight than what I had been wearing; it also gave me a silver
saber, and so I wore the Sokoban AoR and #twoweaponed. Donations got my 
naked AC to zero, and now I was feeling pretty good, except for having to 
deal with Yeenoghu still. I did some polypiling and got a magic marker (the
only one I didn't wish for all game) --- blessed up Stormy and my daggers,
got my AC to -22, and decided to take on the Quest. Oh, my polypile also
got me a bag of holding. Finally! Awesome! This made looting the Quest so 
much easier.

I had been having trouble figuring out how to finish the quest; most
people recommended Xorn polying as opposed to a cursed potion of gain
level, and I couldn't get holy water even after two confused scrolls of
remove curse, but I found a better solution (or at least, what I think
was a better solution). I jumped down and got in the right area on my
first try, peppered the Master Assassin full of daggers, picked up the
Key and the Bell, and then took from my bag --- an uncursed scroll of
teleport and five tripe rations. Having come up with this method myself
(I haven't seen it in any spoilers) made me very proud of myself, not 
that it makes up for some of my sloppy play both earlier and later in 
the game.

Yeenoghu gated in Jubilex, but neither of them even laid a finger on me.
It was really kind of sad. I hit the Medusa level with no means of
levitation, and so I went back up to my stash and polypiled a whole
lot more. I couldn't get a ring of levitation, but I did get a whole
lot of useful things, including conflict, free action, and blessed +2
increase damage, which I wore when I had nothing better to do. I also
got a whole lot more holy water and some scrolls, but no magic markers
and no wands of death. (A wand of death on a soldier in the Castle and
Orcus were the only ones I got ever, but they were enough.) I think
the biggest win was turning four blessed scrolls of something stupid
(light maybe) into four blessed scrolls of charging.

After running out of rings I didn't want to polypile, I dug down from
Medusa, went up, killed Medusa, and found a shield of reflection (useless,
I had one in my bag) and levitation boots in Perseus's statue. Excellent!
Conflict made the castle easy, I found a silver dragon who dropped
scales for me, and the wand was 0:3. Wished up boots of speed (never
saw others all game) as I hadn't found a quantum mechanic to eat yet,
and my boots of jumping weren't doing much for me. (I think I just don't
know how to use them, but I jumped maybe twice all game.) I also wished
for another AoLS, and here's another mistake that is silly rather than
horrible: I took off my AoR to put it on, and said "Oh no, I have to stop
twoweaponing and get my shield of reflection back out," and did this for
a couple thousand turns, _even though I was wearing SDSM._ The other two
wishes I used went to magic markers, my AC became -34, and +7 Stormy,
+5 silver saber, and 14 +5 daggers proved more than adequate.

I think the time it took me from the VoTD to ascension was less than four
hours...  maybe three and a half? I credit much of this to buying up a ton
of clairvoyance from the VoTD priest, some of it to the mysterious force
loving me, and some to playing, if sloppily, quickly. Also, intelligent
use of the many wands of digging minotaurs dropped played a role.

I had already done some alchemy, but in Vlad's tower I did a whole
bunch more, and ended up with quite the max HP. I decided to raise my
max HP through alchemy rather than level-gains or nurses because nurses
are dengerous and fickle, and level-gains increase the difficulty of
randomly-generated monsters.  I must have consumed 20 blessed potions
of full healing. With the Master Key of Thievery, 330HP is pretty
ridiculous. I also polypiled up four or five more amulets of lifesaving
(!!!).

The wizard fell to a cockatrice corpse that was in the zoo downstairs,
and then I was off! A cursed scroll of teleport brought me _right next
to_ the VS, and I performed the ritual. As I was about to descend, a
cockatrice spawned next to me. I killed it, picked it up, and said "Oh
yeah, the Sanctum is not going to be a problem." Down the stairs! I WAS
BURDENED. Goodbye AoLS number three. The Sanctum was in fact a cakewalk
though, cursed potion of gain level up (it was sitting around Orcus-town),
and the mysterious force was very kind. My wands of death were enough to
take out the Wizard all three times he came back, and I got up to Earth
pretty quickly. The portal was like ten squares over (I had learned light
or something that I had forgotten by now, and magic markers had scored me
gold detection), and then Air! Air was really weak sauce with the MKoT.
I think I gained HP inside of air elementals a couple of times. Fire
was also really easy, and then water, which has made my life miserable
a couple of times, was _also_ really easy, because I just levitated over
everything and found the portal in <100 moves.

Astral--- well, I was planning not to use Conflict this time, as once
this had killed me, and on my previous ascension, it had nearly killed 
me---  but I _forgot to take off my ring of levitation_. Much better 
would have been increase damage. But it turned out not to be a problem,
as Pestilence fell to the wand of death, angels and priests fell to my 
weapon combination, and the first altar I tried was the right one. The
lowest I got was 243 HP.

Some random facts of note:

 * I had intended not to genocide L, until one cursed my blindfold and I
   decided to exact brutal vengeance.
 * I though about not genociding h, but I wanted to ascend, not be hardcore.
 * This was my first time ever playing a rogue, with the possible exception
   of getting rogue randomly once or twice in my first week of playing the
   game.
 * This was the first time I made it to Gehennom without genociding ;. 
   The ring of free action is awesome.

I really think reading this group for the past few months has improved
my play significantly. Thanks, all!

